\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces C1-gated stochastic resonance dissociation. \textbf  {Left:} Qwen~7B (collinearity 0.973, C1 met)---noise produces a dramatic inverted-U, lifting composition from 8.7\% to 99.3\% vs.\ task arithmetic (+90.7 points). \textbf  {Right:} Qwen~0.5B (collinearity 0.906, C1 not met)---noise produces no meaningful benefit (+2.0 points at best) and degrades monotonically. The dissociation confirms that condition C1 (suboptimality) gates the stochastic resonance effect, ruling out regularization (falsification condition F4).}}{33}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c1_dissociation}{{1}{33}{C1-gated stochastic resonance dissociation. \textbf {Left:} Qwen~7B (collinearity 0.973, C1 met)---noise produces a dramatic inverted-U, lifting composition from 8.7\% to 99.3\% vs.\ task arithmetic (+90.7 points). \textbf {Right:} Qwen~0.5B (collinearity 0.906, C1 not met)---noise produces no meaningful benefit (+2.0 points at best) and degrades monotonically. The dissociation confirms that condition C1 (suboptimality) gates the stochastic resonance effect, ruling out regularization (falsification condition F4)}{figure.1}{}}
